  "interpretation": "Four preselected V48 cases are all retained, without filtering by stage direction or size. R means V39 original; C means V46 candidate. Absolute nonnegative stage durations are distinct from query C-minus-R deltas and within-arm position32-minus-position33 contrasts. Stage gap equals (C32-R32)-(C33-R33)=(C32-C33)-(R32-R33). Signed arm terms are C=(C32-C33), R=-(R32-R33). Alignment uses the stage gap sign. Each case has its own positive-support denominator; these shares are not fractions of total elapsed time and are not aggregated across cases. More arm support does not mean that arm is globally slower or its timer is an outlier. No temporal rise, fall or spike is inferred from four cells. These are previously exposed, non-simultaneous wall-time records; the arithmetic does not establish decoder, CPU, I/O, scheduler or host-load causality."
